id: core/articulation-floor
title: "the articulation floor: seal, answer, reveal, reason"
kind: measurement-protocol
record_shape: header
status: draft
spec_version: "articulation-floor.0.1"
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-13; from Dave's /polanyi design (surface, records, loop), restated onto the kernel and improved where the tree contradicted it; the improvements are marked"
updated: 2026-09-13

purpose: >
  Measure how much of what a principal knows their records could say in
  advance. The instrument is the question card that already exists: nothing new
  is built in front of the person. What changes is what the card does before it
  renders and after it is answered. The bot seals a prediction of the answer and
  of the reason; the person answers; the seal is revealed and scored; the
  person scores the sealed reason. The rolling reason accuracy per axis is the
  floor. Its curve, read over time, is the finding.

one_principle: >
  The question card you already have is the instrument. A /polanyi page is not
  a new page type; it is a Yawn whose questions happen to be Polanyi's axes,
  rendered through the same card (question-packets/polanyi.yawn).

kernel_mapping:
  rule: >
    This loop is a specialization of the movement loop, not a second loop.
    signal -> orientation -> choice -> move -> proof -> update
    (core/movement-loop.yawn) becomes: question selected -> seal written ->
    answer given -> reveal compared -> reason checked -> floor updated. The
    seal is the prediction the proof contract already asks for before a move
    (schemas/record-proof-receipt.v1.schema.json: prediction, verifier,
    falsifier); the reveal is the "replayed comparison between expectation and
    result" that core/proof-and-boundary.yawn already lists as a form of
    proof; the reason check is the falsifier applied to the reason, not the
    answer.
  beats:
    - beat: 1
      name: seal
      kernel: prediction (before the move)
      when: at question selection, never at render
      who: the bot, or the record that already carries an attributed prediction
      record: templates/seal.yawn
      rule: "No seal, no question. A question rendered without a valid seal is content, not a measurement."
    - beat: 2
      name: answer
      kernel: move
      when: the card as today; candidates plus freeform, freeform always available
      who: the principal
      record: templates/answer.yawn
    - beat: 3
      name: reveal
      kernel: proof (replayed comparison between expectation and result)
      when: immediately after the answer; the one designed moment of motion on the page
      scoring: "hit | partial | miss; a pick is scored by comparison and is hit or miss only; freeform is scored by the principal"
    - beat: 4
      name: reason
      kernel: falsifier on the reason
      when: one tap after the reveal, on the SEALED reason, never a fresh one
      scoring: "yes | partly | no"
      rule: "Mandatory. A card that skips beat 4 emits an incomplete record; an incomplete record never enters the floor."

records:
  seal:
    template: templates/seal.yawn
    written_at: selection
    hashed: "sha256 over canonical JSON of question, axis, predicted_answer, predicted_reason, confidence, model, t_sealed (lib/articulation-floor-v0.1.mjs sealHash)"
    append_only: true
    where_seals_exist_today:
      - "question-packets/polanyi.yawn: one seal per axis, blind, written by the agent from the records it cites"
      - "records/yawn.bot-state.yawn: one seal per queued decision, generated by scripts/render-bot-state.mjs from the decision's attributed recommendation and reasoning; anchored (blind false) because the question-first contract shows the recommendation beside the candidates"
  answer:
    template: templates/answer.yawn
    closes_only_with: reason_match
    re_ask: "an answer with prior_answer set; drift lives on it, not in its own record"
  floor:
    template: templates/floor.yawn
    one_per: "axis, plus one global (axis: all)"
    recomputed_by: "lib/articulation-floor-v0.1.mjs computeFloor over the closed answers; the live record is records/articulation-floor.yawn"
    the_number_that_matters: reason_accuracy
  polanyi:
    packet: question-packets/polanyi.yawn
    rule: "each axis is a question and goes through the same four beats; the bot seals a prediction of the reader's mark before the reader sets it, so the page measures itself"

verification:
  provenance_check: >
    The design named a dave/provenance module to verify t_sealed < t_answered
    on every record. In this tree that role is scripts/validate-articulation-floor-v0.1.mjs
    (shape, hash, order, replay of the floor) and the semantic validators in
    lib/articulation-floor-v0.1.mjs, which the runtime can port; dave/ holds
    mental models, not modules. Improvement marked.
  ranking: >
    The design named a dave/lacuna ranker by expected information gain. The
    kernel's selector is core/inquiry-selection.yawn; its semantic_priority
    pass already carries expected_information_value and
    orientation_gain_per_effort. Selection writes the seal, so the ranker
    never sees the answer. No second ranker is created. Improvement marked.

loop_rules:
  - "Never interrupt. Questions land in the pulse and in the drawer; no modals mid-task. This keeps the surface in reintegrating mode rather than destructive mode, and it is the whole reason a cadence setting exists."
  - "Re-ask gap: 21 days by default, tunable (lib REASK_GAP_DAYS_DEFAULT). Any answered question becomes eligible after the gap. Re-asks are capped at one in five questions per pulse."
  - "Seal precedes render, always. Enforced by the validator; a runtime enforces it by refusing to render a question without a valid seal."
  - "Reason check is mandatory. No record closes without beat 4."
  - "Selection feeds it. The seal is written at selection, so the ranker never sees the answer."
  - "Blind or anchored, say which. A seal that was visible before the answer (a shown recommendation) is anchored; the floor counts blind_n and anchored_n separately, and an anchored floor measures agreement, not prediction."
  - "Public is not unsealed. In a public repository a seal can be read before the answer; the hash protects the guess from being changed after the answer, not from being seen. A reader who looks first has anchored their own answer and should say so."

readout:
  rule: "reason_accuracy is the number that matters; answer_accuracy on its own is correlation. Below ten closed records the floor is reported, not read (lib FLOOR_MIN_N)."
  table:
    - curve: "rises, plateaus above 0"
      verdict: floor-measured
      meaning: "Polanyi proved for this domain. The plateau is the floor, measured."
    - curve: "rises toward 1.0"
      verdict: refuted-for-domain
      meaning: "Polanyi refuted for this domain: what is known can be said."
    - curve: "rises, plateaus, breaks upward after an ontology change"
      verdict: extension-after-break
      meaning: "The floor is a property of the representation, not of knowledge. This is the bet."
    - curve: "answer_accuracy high, reason_accuracy low"
      verdict: correlation-not-articulation
      meaning: "Correlation, not articulation. Polanyi keeps the point. Check for confabulation before claiming anything."
  executable: "lib/articulation-floor-v0.1.mjs readFloor"

public_slice:
  where: https://yawn.bot/status
  shows: "one block per pulse: the global floor and one row per measured axis, n and reason accuracy, updated every pulse; when an axis breaks upward after an ontology change, last_break links the change and the block marks it"
  source_record: records/articulation-floor.yawn
  honesty: "a floor with n zero is shown as n zero; nothing is backfilled and nothing is invented"

glyphs:
  rule: "five, pixel-native, inside the existing type; no new icons in the nav"
  table:
    - glyph: "∘→●"
      meaning: "from -> to; subsidiary into focal; the one glyph that carries the theory; faint, on every card"
    - glyph: "[■]"
      meaning: "sealed; shown only in the reveal, marking what was locked"
    - glyph: "● ◈ ◇"
      meaning: "hit, partial, miss; green, lime, red in the runtime's existing palette (it has no yellow; lime is its yellow)"
    - glyph: "├─◇──●─┤"
      meaning: "axis; ◇ Polanyi's mark, ● yours; on /polanyi only"
    - glyph: "↺"
      meaning: "re-ask; marks a question seen before"

constraints:
  - "header untouched, sidebar untouched"
  - "neon default, existing palette, existing pixel type, no new typeface"
  - "mobile first: the reveal split holds at 380px and stacks below"
  - "reduced motion: the card turn becomes a crossfade"
  - "the reason check is three buttons, sentence case, no icons"

build_order:
  rule: "smallest first; each step ships alone and is useful alone"
  steps:
    - step: 1
      move: "write the seal before render: one function in the question pipeline"
      done_here: "scripts/render-bot-state.mjs seals every queued decision; question-packets/polanyi.yawn seals every axis"
      why_first: "it cannot be backfilled; every day waited costs data that can never be recovered"
    - step: 2
      move: "add beat 4: three buttons after the answer, emit reason_match"
      done_here: "templates/answer.yawn requires it; the runtime surface is the product repository's"
    - step: 3
      move: "emit the floor each pulse and show it on /status"
      done_here: "records/articulation-floor.yawn at n zero; the runtime reads it"
    - step: 4
      move: "create the polanyi Yawn: seven axis questions; everything above runs on it unchanged"
      done_here: "question-packets/polanyi.yawn"

improvements_over_the_design:
  - "seal source: for a decision question the attributed recommendation already is the prediction, written and committed before any answer; the renderer seals it without a provider call, so step 1 starts today for every open decision"
  - "blind versus anchored: the runtime shows the recommendation beside the candidates by contract, so a decision's seal is not hidden; the record says so and the floor keeps the two counts apart instead of pretending"
  - "axes: the six categories the design named do not exist as question categories in either repository; the axis is the packet question_key or the decision's own axis, which the records already carry"
  - "provenance and ranking modules: mapped onto the validator and core/inquiry-selection.yawn rather than creating dave/provenance and dave/lacuna, which would have been a second ranker and a module inside the mental-models folder"
  - "where answers persist is not decided here; it is the open question the runtime filed (questions/open-questions.yawn), extended for answer records"

open_questions_ref: questions/open-questions.yawn

boundary:
  - "A seal is a prediction, an answer is the principal's, a floor is a measurement; none is authority, diagnosis, or truth."
  - "A hit does not mean the bot understood the person; a miss does not mean the person was wrong."
  - "The loop never interrupts, never ratifies a decision, and never fills choice: in a decision record."
  - "The floor is a property of the representation under test; it is never a claim about the person's worth."

links:
  - question-packets/polanyi.yawn
  - schemas/articulation-floor.v0.1.schema.json
  - templates/seal.yawn
  - templates/answer.yawn
  - templates/floor.yawn
  - records/articulation-floor.yawn
  - records/yawn.bot-state.yawn
  - core/movement-loop.yawn
  - core/proof-and-boundary.yawn
  - core/inquiry-selection.yawn
  - questions/open-questions.yawn

proof:
  covers:
    - records
    - loop_rules
    - readout
  validator: scripts/validate-articulation-floor-v0.1.mjs
  tests:
    - tests/articulation-floor-v0.1.test.mjs
    - tests/render-bot-state.test.mjs
  fixture: fixtures/articulation-floor.v0.1.json
  condition: >
    The fixture ledger validates by shape, semantics, and replay; every seal in
    question-packets/polanyi.yawn and records/yawn.bot-state.yawn recomputes to
    its hash; an answer before its seal, an edited seal, a record without
    reason_match, a pick scored partial, and a floor that does not replay all
    fail closed; the readout returns the table's verdicts.
  falsifier: >
    A question is rendered with no seal or a seal whose hash does not
    recompute; an answer closes without beat 4; a floor is shown that the
    ledger does not reproduce; or a surface shows a verdict below ten records.
  not_covered:
    - "the runtime surface (reveal, reason buttons, glyphs, motion, 380px) lives in the product repository and is proved there"
    - "never interrupt, the re-ask cap, and the pulse cadence are stated here and enforced by no validator yet"
    - "whether the seven Polanyi marks are the right reading of the sources"
  status: contract-defined
